*
!README.md
!.gitignore
# This is quite possibly the only symlink I'd ever put into git tracking here
# Because it's:
# 1) Easily spelled via relative symlink (`ln -s . "$(basename "$PWD")"`)
# 2) Doesn't require `../../..` to get back to ~
# 3) Always useful as long as pj-quick-access is useful
# 4) Allows `pj pj` to work (this is incredibly satisfying, but also a bit gimmicky)
!pj-quick-access
